  "accepted_mathematical_interfaces": [
    "The literal aLin,aAnti,dblZ,dblz,dblz-prime,kZero,letterDir and slab conventions match the original IsSystem40-108. The sign kappa=-i c gives positive Im Z, including distinct nonorthogonal frames.",
    "For W=(L^-1 S L)^t G, WG^-1W=W*G^-1W*=G implies W(W+W*)^-1G+G(W+W*)^-1W=G, with the SAME W in both summands. The mixed-row equations give SM=MS. Multiplication by L^-t and A^-1 proves exactly kappa/(8i)(SN+NS)=M. This identity is now explicit in the proof.",
    "Balanced quadratic exponentials are the original opposite-row contraction operators. Harmonicity kills them under ordinary differentiation; letterDir is a coordinate insertion with no extra scalar. At an orthonormal frame the Gaussian is c_x exp(sum pi(-Im kappa) z w), giving the exact factorial and positive Fischer norm.",
    "On the opposite triangular cell, strictly lower coordinates have positive weights for a strictly increasing linear functional. The fixed left-torus/right-Borel eigenspace is therefore one-dimensional. The domain is connected by indefinite Gram--Schmidt, so local uniqueness gives the exact principal-minor formula globally.",
    "The two definite blocks of a unitary matrix have singular values at least one. Exterior-power and complementary-minor identities bound every leading minor by the pth minor. The original cumulative weights telescope to decay at least |Delta_p|^-n; no weight or exponent was changed.",
    "The full complex-matrix slab, not only its orthonormal locus, is parametrized by y=x0 g b(H), with H in a compact Hermitian neighborhood of J. Its Lebesgue density is j_x0(H) dg dH, positive and bounded, because original left unitary translation has real determinant one. Thus the exact full-matrix Jacobian is retained.",
    "The matrix-ball Jacobian gives determinant(I-Z*Z)^-r. Multiplication by |Delta_p|^-n gives exponent n/2-r>=0 on a bounded ball, including n=2r. Compact definite endpoints and r=0 are separately valid.",
    "The probability diagonal-torus average preserves the original Lebesgue slab integral and projects any bounded-invariant-norm holomorphic section to F(x0)K(y,x0)/K(x0,x0). Absolute L1 and boundedness justify Fubini and L2. The exact positive scalar is integral_slab |K(y,x0)|^2 / K(x0,x0), uniformly in F and x for each fixed datum and delta."
